# One package, explicit layers

Odroe is a composable full-stack framework for Dart and Flutter products. It
keeps the application model shared, then places platform-specific code at the
runtime boundary.

```dart
App(
  modules: <Module>[
    QueryModule(),
    RpcModule.http(),
    DocumentModule(),
    RouterModule(routes: routeTree),
  ],
  builder: (app) => Product(router: app.read(routerKey)),
)
```

## What is available

- A small application container with deterministic module disposal.
- Typed filesystem routing without annotations or `build_runner`.
- Query and mutation state for Dart and Flutter.
- Typed RPC and adapter-neutral HTTP server contracts.
- Semantic Document rendering, SSR, SSG, and Flutter Web handoff.
- Renderer-neutral MDC and filesystem-backed Press collections.
- Typed relational SQL plus explicit SQLite, PostgreSQL, MySQL/MariaDB, and
  D1 drivers.
- Dart VM server artifacts for local hosts and containers.

## What stays explicit

Odroe does not install a global database, transport, router, or cache. Import
the product entrypoint you need and install only the corresponding module.

Runtime support is documented as a matrix, not implied by a package name.
SQLite and PostgreSQL are verified. D1 and MySQL/MariaDB remain Preview with
documented limits. Edge Fetch has required Node coverage and an optional local
Workerd integration; it has not been remotely deployed.

| Product target | Artifact | Status | Current evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Flutter Android, iOS, and Web | Flutter build | Verified locally | Example source builds Web, Android release APK, and unsigned iOS release in generated host scaffolds; no signed or device release claim |
| Semantic Document and SSG | `build/web` | Verified locally | Real route rendering and prerender integration |
| Native server | Dart VM executable | Verified locally | Runs on the build OS and architecture |
| Cloudflare | Worker plus static assets | Preview | Required compiled Node smoke; optional local Workerd integration; no remote deployment claim |

Database support has its own provider-by-provider evidence and limits.

